# General back‑propagation formulas (for any layer i)

Given the forward equations
    z_i = W_i a_(i−1) + b_i
    a_i = f_i(z_i)

and an incoming gradient  dL/da_i  from the layer above,
the backward computations are:

1. Through the activation
       dL/dz_i = (dL/da_i) ⊙ f_i'(z_i)

2. Parameter gradients
       dL/dW_i = (dL/dz_i) a_(i−1)ᵀ
       dL/db_i = dL/dz_i             

3. Propagate gradient to previous layer
       dL/da_(i−1) = W_iᵀ (dL/dz_i)